-- The firmware counterpart's machine: QEMU's micro:bit, whose nRF51822
-- Cortex-M0 the lanes run on.  This describes the emulator's map, not a
-- board refine supports, and only the lane's entry-module file,
-- lanes/lane-microbit.ldn, imports it.  It names the core and the table's
-- length, the constrained reference's, and, beside this file, the memory;
-- no interrupt is named, since the counterpart takes SysTick's alone.

compiler.device("microbit")
compiler.core("cortex-m0")
compiler.vectors(48)
